target: cmd/looper/main.go
verify: go test ./cmd/looper/ -count=1 -run 'TestPushCheck'
expect: a missing -run-id gave exit
why:    required, not optional. In the Python both record-derived blockers were computed only when --run-id was present, so OMITTING it turned off the owed-report check and the broken-outcome check at once — while a BOGUS id was correctly caught as an unknown run. The cheapest wrong spelling was therefore the one that passed, and the run pushed on nothing. (Anchored through the error text, which names this subcommand: `if *runID == "" {` alone now occurs twice.)
--- old
	if *runID == "" {
		return errors.New("push-check: -run-id is required — without it the record's outcome and " +
			"the report check are both invisible, and the run pushes on nothing")
	}
--- new
	if false {
		return errors.New("push-check: -run-id is required — without it the record's outcome and " +
			"the report check are both invisible, and the run pushes on nothing")
	}
